WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.530
Hi! Today we'll meet four-digit numbers. We'll learn place value, and how to read and write numbers all the way up to 10 000.

2
00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:18.042
Look at 3762. From the left, the places are thousands, hundreds, tens and ones.

3
00:00:18.192 --> 00:00:24.042
The 3 is in the thousands place, so it stands for 3 thousands, which is 3000.

4
00:00:24.192 --> 00:00:30.186
The 7 is in the hundreds place, so it stands for 7 hundreds, which is 700.

5
00:00:30.336 --> 00:00:38.706
So 3762 is 3000 plus 700 plus 60 plus 2.

6
00:00:38.856 --> 00:00:46.098
We read from the biggest place. 2691 is two thousand, six hundred and ninety-one.

7
00:00:46.248 --> 00:00:52.074
In 4305, the tens digit is 0. That means there are no tens.

8
00:00:52.224 --> 00:00:56.946
When we write a number, we put a 0 in any place that has nothing.

9
00:00:57.096 --> 00:01:05.658
The greatest four-digit number is 9999. Add 1 and we get ten thousand, 10 000.

10
00:01:05.808 --> 00:01:14.634
Watch out! Some pupils write 4 thousands, 3 hundreds and 5 ones as 435. That's wrong!

11
00:01:14.784 --> 00:01:21.930
There are no tens, but we still write 0 in the tens place. The correct number is 4305.

12
00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:28.986
When you finish, count the digits. A four-digit number must have four digits.

13
00:01:29.136 --> 00:01:38.994
Your turn! In 3762, which place is the 7 in? Pause and think.

14
00:01:39.144 --> 00:01:46.842
The 7 is in the hundreds place. It stands for 700. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:46.992 --> 00:01:56.946
Another one! What is 2000 plus 600 plus 90 plus 1? Pause and think.

16
00:01:57.096 --> 00:02:03.858
The answer is 2691. Did you get it right?

17
00:02:04.008 --> 00:02:13.074
Here's another! What is the value of the 8 in 8150? Pause and think.

18
00:02:13.224 --> 00:02:20.466
The 8 is in the thousands place, so its value is 8000. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:20.616 --> 00:02:30.258
Try one more! What number has 6 thousands, 2 tens and 9 ones? Pause and think.

20
00:02:30.408 --> 00:02:40.194
There are no hundreds, so we write 0 in the hundreds place. The answer is 6029. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:40.344 --> 00:02:49.338
Last one! How do we write five thousand and eighty in numerals? Pause and think.

22
00:02:49.488 --> 00:02:57.858
5 thousands, no hundreds, 8 tens and no ones. We write 5080. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:58.008 --> 00:03:08.538
Remember: a four-digit number has thousands, hundreds, tens and ones from left to right. Read from the biggest place, and write 0 for any empty place.

24
00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:15.522
Today, look for a four-digit number around you and say what each digit stands for!

